            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "NDLEWIS"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I tried this recipe for Christmas dinner and it was absolutely delicious - EVERYONE went back for seconds, even my husband who normally doesn't care for gelatin dishes."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Thanks Grace, this one is a winner. Attractive, easy to make, festive and delicious! I used a ring gelatin mold and decorated the platter with fresh whole strawberries. Used regular Cool Whip. Next time will try lite Cool Whip to make it a little less decadent. \r\nRecipe can easily serve 10-12 without skimping on portion size. Don't expect leftovers!",
            "datePublished": "2004-05-03T19:35:14.523Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Vicky Gunkel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is one of my favorite jello salads for holidays. Everyone loves it and I never have left overs. I have also substituted strawberries and strawberry jello, as well as peaches and peach jello with wonderfully light and creamy results but I think pear lime is the overall favorite!",
            "datePublished": "2005-03-18T20:31:53.187Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "zoesmom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was SOOOOO good! Creamy and sweet. I used sugar free jello, reduced fat cream cheese, and lite cool whip. My husband who can't stand anything \"light\" loved this!! WOW!",
            "datePublished": "2005-11-27T12:34:37.527Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I was trying to find a recipe I could make for sugar free for my brother. \r\n This one worked great. I used sugar free jello, the pears that are in\r\n pear juice and I used real whipping cream sweetened with fructose. \r\n Thank you for the recipe. \r\nKathy in Alaska",
            "datePublished": "2002-07-26T18:16:29.403Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "TVOSE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Probably would not have added the entire container of cool whip....3/4 would have been perfect.",
            "datePublished": "2002-10-24T14:50:20.013Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "AUNTSHEL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very refreshing! I loved the texture and it was very easy to make. This will be a repeat recipe for sure! I think it would also be great with different flavors of jello as well such as cherry or orange or even strawberry.",
            "datePublished": "2004-08-04T23:00:36.520Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jocelyn Kent"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mom and I have been making this recipe for years and it is my favorite. However, we make it a little differently. Heat the pear juice and lime gelatin the same. In a blender combine the pears, 2-8 ounce packages of cream cheese blend until smooth. Whip 1 cup whipping cream, fold it into the jello mixture. Pour into mold and refridgerate for several hours. It is delicious.",
            "datePublished": "2009-11-22T09:13:36.630Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GG"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I make this for all the holidays without the milk, of course, there is no need for that! And we put in a 2.75qt rectangular glass pyrex dish with a lid, no need to worry about releasing a mold. Also, I heat all the pear juice then add the jello to the pan until dissolved, no need to mess another bowl and put the pan in the fridge to cool until syrupy, then add the mashed pears &amp; cool whip right in the pan blend until mixed thoroughly. Then transfer to the pyrex dish. You only need to wash one pan &amp; utensils used. Everyone loves it!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-11-30T17:31:26.057Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a good tasting jello salad that looks pretty on a nice serving plate. Next time I make this salad I am going to buy an extra can of pears and cut them into small squares to use as garnish around the outside of the salad. Thanks Grace!",
            "datePublished": "2003-12-02T09:36:39.623Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sue L"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We love this... Can also be done with crushed pineapple... you may need to buy extra unsweetened pineapple juice for the juice step. There are different ways to cut calories... buy sugar-free Jello, use neufchatel cream cheese, any fruit/juice you use can be \"in natural juices\" instead of the sugar/syrup kind... You do not have to make it in a mold (I never do)... Chill in a pretty serving bowl or cut ‘square’ individual servings, placed onto a lettuce leaf... Um, it can be served as a ‘salad’ that way... or, a light dessert . Also nicely complements a BBQ/picnic :)",
            "datePublished": "2019-03-14T13:57:30.247Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GoldFig6999"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My kids called this sea scum salad but they loved it. I would also make it with cherry jello, which my kids, brats they were, called Blood in the Water and liked to have with iceberg lettuce salad and submarine sandwiches. For dessert we had blue jello with gummy bears stuck in it and whip cream \"iceberg\" on top. We ate this when we watched Jaws or Titanic.",
            "datePublished": "2026-05-18T02:38:59.737Z"
          },
